----------------------------------------------------------------------
Source:    https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code
License:   MIT (full text: vendor/ecc/LICENSE)
Bundled:   vendor/ecc/ (provenance files) plus the skills/agents/commands
           snapshot installed under workbench/.claude/ (27 skills, 16 agents,
           14 commands selected from the pinned revision)
Pin:       commit 928076cc08cbb31e8549cea2883b4f51811de1c8
           (upstream tag v2.0.0-rc.1, dated 2026-05-25)

Why a pinned snapshot instead of "latest":
  1. Reproducibility — an installer whose payload moves upstream cannot be
     regression-tested. The pin makes every install byte-identical.
  2. Reviewability — the snapshot was reviewed for machine-specific paths,
     secrets, and unsafe auto-executing hooks before inclusion.
  3. Known compatibility risk — upstream may have published fixes after
     2026-05-25. At the time of this RC the maintainer's network could not
     reach github.com (TLS handshake failure through the local proxy), so
     "current stable" could not be re-verified online. Before v1.0 the pin
     MUST be re-checked against upstream and either bumped or re-justified.
     Track: RELEASE_READINESS.md, gate G7.

What was NOT taken from ECC:
  - The Node.js hook runtime (per-tool-call spawn cost conflicts with the
    token budget; the self-developed Python gate replaces that function).
  - Install scripts and profiles (this distribution has its own installer).

